a.keep('B07','Both short connectors end in slight turns without complete heads. The final target has a D stem and loop followed by a tiny low oval zero; its small scale does not justify changing it. Codim has no separate point, and the final sentence point is visible.')
a.keep('B09','The written number has 1, two-lobed 8 and oval 0. The connector is the same one-sided terminal form as above, so the doubt remains; codim has no point before the final d.')
a.keep('B10','Two larger initial forms survive beneath the oblique cancellations, with the right one showing a bowl-like double return. NB remains favored over Et; a clean Le/les would not account for the larger second form. The cancellation prevents a definitive reading.')
a.keep('B11','Both readings propose the same parenthesized 181 beneath the strike. The middle numeral is crossed and remains tentative; moving the uncertainty wrapper outside the parentheses does not change the reading.')
a.keep('B13','The raised upright and separate dot make a bang, not a prime. Both small subscripts share the reduced x form used for the point introduced just above; there is no independently established n in this definition. The broad powerset P and wave-plus-bar relation remain as recorded, with the outer closing parenthesis separate.')
a.change('B14',r'\deleted{qui} \deleted{Considérons les} on a aussi','The cancelled first word has a q descender and dotted i. The next initial C is distinctly taller than the adjacent low o/n body and is retained as a capital. In the live continuation, the long low au group is followed by two s-like returns and a final dotted i; aussi is favored over ainsi, which would require an earlier i dot.')
