a.keep('B15','The number retains a narrow 1, the two loops of 8, and a curved terminal 2 with a descending return. No additional cancellation crosses the number; 182 is retained.')
a.keep('B16','The initial noun ends in a low return beyond germe, supporting germes. The shortened rev. has an initial shoulder, low e/v joins and a separate point; it is not the broader mor. shape. The written covering base is D1, even though the fibre notation motivates a mathematical query. The very faint horizontal trace below is unlike the dark writing and is not promoted to punctuation.')
a.keep('B17','The three chain edges have visible directional ends. The tiny mark beneath can has an angular entry and low foot like the neighboring numeral 1, but remains compatible with 4; it is not a securely closed a. The third object subscript is overtraced. The older crossed cluster has two short parallel strokes and a D-like remnant; =Dd remains tentative rather than being replaced by a clean X.')
a.keep('B18','The label has a dotted i and a lower d. Strong crossing diagonals form the live X over a visible older D; the old lower-right mark remains doubtful. Omitting the live X would mistake the replacement for cancellation alone.')
a.change('B19',r'les \deleted{$x_i$} \unsure{images|germes} $x_i$ de $x$','The left crossed symbol has the crossing body of x and a separate low i trace. A g descender and low ending survive in the following word. The preceding low marks can belong either to the compressed ima body or to the adjoining cancellation, so germes cannot be excluded alongside images. The live second x_i and following de x are clear.')
